# Visibility-only CODEOWNERS (OVD-888, parent OVD-854).
#
# GitHub requests review from the listed owners on PRs that touch these paths,
# except that it never requests review from a PR's own author. Agent PRs are
# authored from @optomachina's own account, so for those PRs this file requests
# nobody. It mainly matters for PRs from other authors (for example Hexseeker,
# who has write access), where it requests @optomachina's review.
#
# Branch protection on main does NOT require code-owner review ("Require
# review from Code Owners" stays off). An author cannot approve their own PR,
# so a required owner review would deadlock every PR authored by @optomachina
# that touches these paths.
#
# Revisit this if agent PRs move to a separate bot account; only a distinct
# author identity makes a required review workable.

/.github/ @optomachina
/scripts/ @optomachina

# This file lands with #818. A pattern for a file that does not exist yet is
# valid and starts matching as soon as the file does.
/docs/sensitive-paths.json @optomachina
